{
  "id": "06-the-lunch-no-one-saw",
  "title": "The Lunch No One Saw",
  "tenet": "Seek God's heart",
  "durationMs": 63903,
  "text": "Imagine a girl noticing that her friend always leaves the lunch table when the food comes out. One day she learns why: there is no lunch in her friend's bag. The next morning she brings enough to share. She does not announce it or take a photograph. She simply makes room beside her. When someone later praises another pupil for being generous, she feels a small urge to tell everyone what she has been doing. Then she looks at her friend eating comfortably and lets the moment pass.\n\nSeek God's heart. The world trains us to look for a return: payment, recognition, influence, or the last word. Christ teaches us to give where we cannot be repaid, to forgive, and to love. Trusting God frees us to do good without collecting applause. Generosity is not a bargain that guarantees you more money. It is an act of faith that what matters to God is worth doing, even when nobody else notices.\n\nDo one quiet act of kindness today. Protect the other person's dignity, and let the good be enough. Your Father sees what happens in secret.",
